## Model card

- **Name:** MiniMax M3.1 Flash Preview
- **Short description:** Preview-tier multimodal coding model from MiniMax, released 2026-09-27 as the fast sibling of the MiniMax M3 flagship. It is **not** a renamed M3: a third-party fact-check explicitly warns against reusing M3's architecture figures for M3.1, because MiniMax published no M3.1 model card.
- **Provider / access:** Listed on models.dev as `minimax/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview` (2 providers). **Absent from OpenCode Zen** — I queried `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models` on 2026-09-30 (84 ids): `minimax-m3`, `minimax-m2.7`, `minimax-m2.5` are present, no `minimax-m3.1-*` of any kind. Access is gated to MiniMax Code / Token Plan.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-09-27 per models.dev. Knowledge cutoff is listed as `-` (undocumented) on models.dev; the "knowledge cutoff August 2026" in `Gemini_3.5_Flash_Lite.md` is not supported by any page I could fetch.
- **IDs:** `minimax/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview` (models.dev). This repo's `meta.json` uses `minimax-ai/minimax-m3.1-flash-preview`; no Zen Free ID exists (`noFreeId: true` is correct).
- **Context window:** 1,000,000 total with 512,000 max output per models.dev — third-party catalogue only; no first-party MiniMax spec page confirmed it in my fetches.
- **Modalities:** Text, image, video in; text out (`meta.json`). Not independently confirmed on a first-party card.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-30):** models.dev shows **$0.00 in / $0.00 out**, which reflects the Token Plan / MiniMax Code subscription bundle, **not** a free tier. No public per-token price sheet exists (see exclusion note 3).
- **Architecture:** Closed weights; parameter count for M3.1 undisclosed.

### Raw benchmarks found

**Why this file is excluded** — the negative findings, with sources:

1. **BenchLM** (`benchlm.ai`), re-fetched **today 2026-09-30**: the M3.1 Flash Preview entry is a "Model Specs & Sources" page — every benchmark row reads "Not directly comparable". No numeric score for this ID.
2. **models.dev** (the catalogue OpenCode itself consumes): spec fields only — release date, 1M context, 512K output, closed weights. No eval fields.
3. **AI on Mac fact-check** on the M3.1 line: "MiniMax has not published a public M3.1 model card, an official M3.1 benchmark table, or a verified M3.1 API price sheet", and warns not to copy M3's 428B/23B figures onto M3.1.
4. **MiniMax's own model page** (minimax.io): describes capability claims, effort levels and modality support, **with no numeric benchmark table** for the preview.
5. No OpenCode Zen ID (verified above), so no same-harness Zen-side measurement is possible either.

